# Pacfile -- the Arch Linux counterpart of the Brewfile, installed with `./install.sh --pacman`.
# One package per line. Lines above [aur] come from the official repos (pacman), lines below it
# from the AUR (yay). The Brewfile's npm globals and VS Code extensions are installed from the
# Brewfile itself, so those lists live in one place.
#
# Left out on purpose (macOS-only, or Linux already has it):
#   aerospace -> i3          cmux, iterm2, warp -> ghostty + tmux      maccy -> copyq
#   docker-desktop -> docker (native, no VM)    coreutils -> GNU is the default    duti -> xdg-mime
#   mole -> paccache.timer (pacman-contrib)     xcodegen    neo4j-mcp (no Linux package)
#   neofetch -> fastfetch (neofetch is unmaintained)
#   llama.cpp -> ollama-vulkan (runs on the AMD GPU through Vulkan, no ROCm needed)

